        {
          "say": "Don't share equally. Bigger groups get more.",
          "write": "✗ 15, 15, 15"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Bias and sample size",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A biased sample leans one way. It doesn't represent everyone.",
          "write": "biased = leans one way"
        },
        {
          "say": "Online polls are self-selected. People with strong views reply most.",
          "write": "self-selected"
        },
        {
          "say": "Asking at a gym about exercise is the wrong place.",
          "write": "wrong place or time"
        },
        {
          "say": "A bigger sample doesn't fix bias. 10 thousand biased answers are still biased.",
          "write": "size ≠ fair"
        },
        {
          "say": "Random samples vary a bit. Bigger ones vary less.",
          "write": "sample variability"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Estimating from a sample",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "21 of 60 sampled students catch a bus. That's 0.35.",
          "write": "21 ÷ 60 = 0.35"
        },
        {
          "say": "Multiply by the population. 0.35 times 840 is 294 students.",
          "write": "0.35 × 840 = 294"
        },
        {
          "say": "Fish: 50 tagged. Later 10 of 80 caught are tagged. That's an eighth.",
          "write": "10/80 = 1/8",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y8/maths/samples-and-populations-recapture.svg",
          "alt": "80 fish drawn as dots with 10 tagged fish shaded"
        },
        {
          "say": "So 50 is an eighth of all the fish. About 400 fish.",
          "write": "50 × 8 = 400"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Remember",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Stir before you taste. Choose at random.",
          "write": "random = fair",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
